<description>
Complete the repeating pattern through the placeholder suffix, then shift it one column left.

Input structure
- The grid contains a single placeholder color forming the union of bottom suffix rows and right suffix columns.
- The remaining top-left block is a repeated rectangular color tile.

Rule
- Infer the minimal tile from the top-left block and extend it over the full input shape.
- Replace each cell by the color one column to its right in that completed repeating pattern.

Key insight
- The placeholder region is not background to preserve; it hides the continuation of the same tile, and all visible tile colors advance by the same horizontal step.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "top-left non-placeholder block containing a repeated rectangular color tile; placeholder color forms the bottom/right suffix",
  "transform": "extend the tile to the full grid and replace every pixel by the color one column to its right in that completed pattern"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 6-20 rows x 6-20 cols, always square [observed]
  tile:
    size: 2 rows x 2-4 cols
    colors: col_period distinct non-placeholder colors; each row is a permutation of the same set
    row_structure: row 1 is a cyclic left-shift of row 0 by 1-2 positions [observed]
  placeholder:
    color: one extra color not in the tile
    shape: L-shaped suffix = union of bottom rows and right columns
    region: cells (r,c) where r >= r_cut OR c >= c_cut; r_cut, c_cut > 0
  block:
    region: top-left r_cut x c_cut sub-grid, filled by tiling the tile periodically
    constraint: r_cut > row_period AND c_cut > col_period (at least 2 full reps per axis)
    suffix_rows: H - r_cut, range 1-9; suffix_cols: W - c_cut, range 1-9
  output:
    same size as input; entire grid tiled with tile shifted 1 column right
    formula: out[r,c] = tile[r % row_period, (c+1) % col_period]
    colors: tile colors only (placeholder removed)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size N x N (6-20)
    2. Choose tile dimensions (2 rows x W_tile cols, W_tile in 2-4); pick W_tile distinct non-zero colors
    3. Build tile row 0 as the color sequence; row 1 as a cyclic left-shift by 1
    4. Build full output grid by tiling with column-shift +1 applied, i.e. out[r,c] = tile[r % 2, (c+1) % W_tile]
    5. Derive input by un-shifting: the underlying pattern is tile[r % 2, c % W_tile]
    6. Choose r_cut (row_period+1 to N-1) and c_cut (col_period+1 to N-1); fill block = top-left r_cut x c_cut with the un-shifted pattern
    7. Pick a placeholder color not in tile colors; fill the L-shaped suffix region (r >= r_cut OR c >= c_cut) with it
    8. The resulting grid is the input; step-4 grid is the output
```
